<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 5 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">The Great Historians</h1><p class="path-tagline">The writers who invented how we remember the past.</p><p class="path-intro">History is itself a human invention, with inventors. This path reads five of them: the Greek who first called his inquiry historia, the exile who dissected power, the Roman hostage who explained Rome to the conquered, China's grand historian, and the North African judge who asked why states rise and fall at all.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Thinker</a> · <a href="/start">the Chronicler</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herodotus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 484–c. 425 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Herodotus</span><span class="path-step-why">The father of history: travel, marvels and the Persian Wars, told so the deeds of men not fade.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thucydides.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 460–c. 400 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Thucydides</span><span class="path-step-why">The Peloponnesian War by a general who fought in it, history as unflinching analysis of power.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/polybius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polybius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 200–c. 118 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Polybius</span><span class="path-step-why">A Greek hostage in Rome who set out to explain, in forty books, how one city conquered his world in fifty-three years.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/sima-qian"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sima-qian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 145–c. 86 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Sima Qian</span><span class="path-step-why">China's grand historian, who chose disgrace over silence to finish the Records that shaped two millennia of Chinese memory.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-khaldun"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-khaldun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Person · 1332–1406</span><span class="path-step-name">Ibn Khaldun</span><span class="path-step-why">The Muqaddimah's author, who made the rise and fall of dynasties a science centuries before sociology had a name.</span></span></a></li></ol>
